 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Saying what you know or think",
     "texto": [
      "**Что** can link verbs such as **знать** (to know), **думать** (to think) and **сказать** (to say) with the information that follows: **Я знаю, что она работает** (I know that she works) and **Я думаю, что он придёт** (I think he will come). In these cases, **что** means «that»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Order and comma",
     "texto": [
      "In these sentences, the comma goes before **что**, which introduces the subordinate information. A conjugated verb follows; the subject can be left out if it is already clear: **Она сказала, что устала** (she said that she was tired; it is clear that she is the one who got tired). In **Что ты читаешь?** (What are you reading?), **что** asks about a thing and means «what»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
